\]

If $J_{i,C}=\emptyset$, we have $b_{i,J,C}^U(x)=0$ for all $x\in U$ and the gaussian sum vanishes. Thus, it suffices to consider $J_{i,C}\neq\emptyset$ for the supremum. Then
\begin{align*}
